##
    Two programs, one project, and a line saying which one begins.

    Both files declare a 'shared model Program'. They are still two different types, because a
    namespace is part of a name — so nothing collides and both are perfectly good programs.

    What an assembly holds is one entry point, so something has to choose, and it is not the
    compiler's to choose: picking for itself would mean picking by the order the sources happen
    to be listed, and swapping two lines here would quietly change which program ran. The
    project says instead, and says it in the file that describes the build.

    Written where a project holds only one program, the line decides nothing and is an opinion
    (PC0236). Left out where a project holds two, the build is refused and both are named
    (PC0234) — see negatives/project/ambiguous-entry.pcp, which is this file without this line.
##

project Observatory
    source Sky.pc
    source Catalog.pc
    source Ranking.pc

    entry Observatory.Cataloging.Program
end project
